    h3 Crafting WCAG 3 for more accessible user experiences
    text (2026-Sep-25)
    text In the W3C blog post , W3C WAI Director  covers some of the stakes and challenges in developing W3C Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 3.
    link "Crafting WCAG 3 for more accessible user experiences" https://www.w3.org/blog/2026/crafting-wcag-3-for-more-accessible-user-experiences/
    link "Shawn Lawton Henry" https://www.w3.org/staff/#shawn
    h3 WCAG 2.2 and 2.1 in French — Authorized translations updated
    text (2026-Sep-22)
    text The French authorized translations of Web Content Accessibility Guidelines () are updated:
    link WCAG https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/
    text is now based on the 12 December 2024 publication of WCAG 2.2.
    link "Règles pour l’accessibilité des contenus web (WCAG) 2.2" https://www.w3.org/Translations/WCAG22-fr/
    text is now based on the 6 May 2025 publication of WCAG 2.1.
    link "Règles pour l’accessibilité des contenus web (WCAG) 2.1" https://www.w3.org/Translations/WCAG21-fr/
    text These translations followed the .
    link "W3C authorized translations process" https://www.w3.org/2005/02/TranslationPolicy
    text Other translations of WAI resources are listed in .
    link "All WAI Translations" https://www.w3.org/WAI/translations/
    text W3C WAI thanks all who contribute to translations, and encourages translations of W3C accessibility standards and resources in all languages. If you might be interested in translating resources, see .
    link "Translating WAI Resources" https://www.w3.org/WAI/about/translating/
    h3 For Review: WCAG 3 Working Draft – September 2026
    text (2026-Sep-10)
    text is updated. The starting place for background, timeline, and up-to-date information is the . For a list of changes in the September 2026 draft and review questions on the conformance model, see .
    link "W3C Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 3.0 Working Draft" https://www.w3.org/TR/wcag-3.0/
    link "WCAG 3 Introduction" /WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/wcag3-intro/
    link "Status: In-progress drafts" /WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/wcag3-intro/#status-in-progress-drafts
    h3 WCAG Evaluation Methodology (WCAG-EM) 2.0 — Note Published
    text (2026-Jul-23)
    text is published as a W3C Group Note. WCAG-EM describes a methodology with a step-by-step process to evaluate how well digital products conform to Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2. WCAG-EM 1 was specifically for testing websites and web pages. WCAG-EM 2 also applies to apps and other digital products. For an introduction to WCAG-EM, see .
    link "WCAG Evaluation Methodology (WCAG-EM) 2.0" https://www.w3.org/TR/wcag-em-2/
    link "WCAG-EM Overview" /WAI/test-evaluate/conformance/wcag-em/
    h3 For Review: WCAG 3 Working Draft – March 2026
    text (2026-Mar-03)
    text is updated. The starting place for background, timeline, and up-to-date information is the . For a list of changes in the March 2026 draft, see .
    link "W3C Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 3.0 Working Draft" https://www.w3.org/TR/wcag-3.0/
    link "WCAG 3 Introduction" /WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/wcag3-intro/
    link "Status: In-progress drafts" /WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/wcag3-intro/#status-in-progress-drafts
    h3 For Review: W3C Accessibility Guidelines Evaluation Methodology (WCAG-EM) 2.0 — First Draft Note
    text (2026-Feb-05)
    text is available as a first Draft Note. WCAG-EM describes a methodology with a step-by-step process to evaluate how well digital products conform to Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2. WCAG-EM 1 is specifically for testing websites and web pages. WCAG-EM 2 also applies to apps and other digital products. For an introduction to WCAG-EM and more information about the WCAG-EM 2 draft, see .
    link "W3C Accessibility Guidelines Evaluation Methodology (WCAG-EM) 2.0" https://www.w3.org/TR/wcag-em-2/
    link "WCAG-EM Overview" https://www.w3.org/WAI/test-evaluate/conformance/wcag-em/
    h3 For Review: Cognitive Accessibility Research Modules — First Draft Notes
    text (2026-Feb-05)
    text are available as first Draft Notes. The documents cover research on accessibility for people with cognitive and learning disabilities for , , , and . They address user needs, accessibility issues, directions for solutions, and areas for further research. We particularly seek input on what might be appropriate to add to these documents, including other relevant research, additional user needs, and the connection between research and priorities for new work in W3C groups. Information on related work is in .
    link "Cognitive Accessibility Research Modules" https://www.w3.org/TR/coga-research-modules/
    link "Voice Systems and Conversational Interfaces" https://www.w3.org/TR/coga-voice/
    link "Technology Assisted Indoor Navigation / Wayfinding" https://www.w3.org/TR/coga-wayfinding/
    link "Online Safety and Wellbeing (Algorithms and Data)" https://www.w3.org/TR/coga-safety/
    link "Supported Decision-Making Online" https://www.w3.org/TR/coga-sdm/
    link "Cognitive Accessibility at W3C" https://www.w3.org/WAI/cognitive/
    link "See All News" /WAI/news/
    link "Subscribe to WAI News" /WAI/news/subscribe/
