    h2 Web Accessibility Perspectives: Video Captions
    text "Captions are the audio information in text that is synchronized with the audio and visual content. Captions are called \"subtitles\" in some regions."
    text Video Captions are essential for people with disabilities and benefit everyone in a variety of situations.
    row
      link "More About Video Captions" /WAI/perspective-videos/captions/
      link "See All Perspectives Videos" /WAI/perspective-videos/
    link "Featured Resource: Making Audio and Video Media Accessible This media resource helps you understand and create captions/subtitles, audio description of visual information, descriptive transcripts, and sign language for media. It introduces user experiences and benefits to organizations. Making Audio and Video Media Accessible" /WAI/media/av/
